    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily create-owner limit rule: **`POST /api/owners` now returns 429 when 100 or more owners already have a `registrationDate` of today.**\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md (mirroring the existing per-city capacity rule), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckDailyOwnerLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`; throws the checked `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count reaches the limit (100). Runs before `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner`, so a rejected request is never persisted.\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 checked exception holding the `DAILY_LIMIT = 100` constant.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the other handlers.\n4. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted a `dailyLimit` step (governed by `transaction`) into `owners.POST.yml` after `cityCapacity`, and registered the escalation YAML at `escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`.\n\nThe pre-existing `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100 today \u2192 101st rejected with 429) and the full suite pass green.",
